$CATEGORY: Q7 - LANGUAGE ELEMENTS

::Q701::
package -   A directory of classes that are related to each other. {TRUE}

::Q702::
library -   A collection of packages and classes that are available for use in other programs.  {TRUE}

::Q703::
import -    A statement that allows programs to use classes defined in other packages. {TRUE}

::Q704::
token -     The smallest unit of source code, such as an individual word, literal value, or symbol.{TRUE}
    
::Q705::
literal -   A value that appears in source code. For example, "Hello" is a string literal.{TRUE}
    
::Q706::
prompt -    A brief message displayed in a print statement that asks the user for input.{TRUE}
    
$CATEGORY: Q8 - LITERAL & CONSTANTS

::Q801:: 
magic number{
    =A number that appears without explanation as part of an expression
    ~A variable, declared as final, whose value cannot be changed
}
   
::Q802::
constant{
    ~A number that appears without explanation as part of an expression
    =A variable, declared as final, whose value cannot be changed
}

::Q803:: 
format string{
    =The string in System.out.printf that specifies the format of the output
    ~A special code that begins with a percent sign and specifies the data type.
}

::Q804:: 
format specifier{
    ~The string in System.out.printf that specifies the format of the output
    =A special code that begins with a percent sign and specifies the data type. 
}
 
::Q805::
stack trace -   An error message that shows the methods that were running when an exception occurs.{TRUE}
    
::Q806::
 type cast -    An operation that converts one data type into another. {TRUE}
    
::Q807::
modulo -        An operation that yields the remainder when one integer is divided by another.{TRUE}
    